        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add daily cost and plan usage history for OpenCode Go",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Adds a \"Plan Usage\" row (hover-expands into 5-hour / weekly / monthly rate-limit history, 3 tabs) for the OpenCode Go provider, matching Codex/Claude's structure.\n- Adds a \"Cost\" row (hover-expands into a daily $ spend chart, reusing the same `CostHistoryChartMenuView` Codex/Claude use) sourced from the local `opencode-go` SQLite history at `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`.\n- The web-sourced fetch strategy best-effort enriches its rolling/weekly percentages with the local daily buckets, since opencode.ai's web API has no daily-granularity endpoint — but skips that local read when the user explicitly selects Web-only source mode, so that choice is actually honored.\n- Fixes a couple of latent bugs found while wiring this up: the merged \"Overview\" row was showing the Cost chart instead of Plan Usage for OpenCode Go, and the daily chart's request count could overcount turns whose cost is split across multiple `step-finish` parts.\n\n## Screenshots\n_I'll attach the before/after screenshots directly on this PR._\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `swift build` (CodexBar, CodexBarCore, CodexBarCLI) — clean\n- [x] New unit tests: local SQLite day-bucketing/window clamp, request-count dedup, Overview-row submenu routing, Plan Usage series for opencodego, menu row ordering (Usage pane → Plan Usage → Cost)\n- [x] Full `swift test` suite — all tests touching the changed files pass; the only failures are pre-existing timing-sensitive PTY/Keychain tests unrelated to this diff\n- [x] `swiftformat --lint` / `swiftlint` clean on all touched files\n- [x] Manually verified in a packaged, signed `CodexBar.app` build against a real `opencode-go` local database\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
